{"Title":"An Act to exempt certain local housing authority executive directors from anti-spiking provisions","BillNumber":"S1613","DocketNumber":"SD180","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MDB0","Name":"Michael D. Brady","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MDB0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-09T11:56:38.467"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MDB0","Name":"Michael D. Brady","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MDB0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-09T11:56:38.4666667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1613/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Brady, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1613) of Michael D. Brady for legislation to exempt certain local housing authority executive directors from anti-spiking provisions.  Public Service.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 5 paragraph (2)(f) of chapter 32 of the General Laws as appearing in the 2018 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting, in line 211, after the word \"law\" the following words:- \"from a modification in the salary schedule for a local housing authority executive director set in the Department of Housing and Community Development guidelines\".\r\n\tSECTION 2. The amended section shall apply to anyone retiring after January 1, 2018.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}